{"addedOn":10,"avgRating":["fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o"],"breadcrumbsHtml":"<a href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117\">OpenEdge Development: ABL Reference</a>\n<span><i class=\"fa fa-angle-right\"></i>\n</span>\n<a href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/ABL-Syntax-Reference.html\">ABL Syntax Reference</a>\n<span><i class=\"fa fa-angle-right\"></i>\n</span>\n<span class=\"active\">OS-CREATE-DIR statement</span>\n","class":"manual","created":1470,"dislikeurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/dislike/310213","html":"<article class=\"hascomments\" data-page=\"bundle:openedge-abl-reference-117/enus/OS-CREATE-DIR-statement.html\" id=\"bundle:openedge-abl-reference-117/enus/OS-CREATE-DIR-statement.html\"><main role=\"main\"><article aria-labelledby=\"ariaid-title1\" class=\"dita\" id=\"OS-CREATE-DIR-statement\" role=\"article\">\n  <h1 class=\"title topictitle1 reference\" id=\"ariaid-title1\">OS-CREATE-DIR statement</h1>\n  \n  <div class=\"body refbody\">\n    <section class=\"section\">\n      <p class=\"p\">Executes an operating system command from within ABL\nthat creates one or more new directories.</p>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"OS-CREATE-DIR-statement__syntax_GC19YB2698598\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d336796e101\">Syntax</h2>\n      \n      <table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"OS-CREATE-DIR-statement__idGDN2OP2673661\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code>OS-CREATE-DIR <strong class=\"ph b synmeta\">{</strong> <var class=\"keyword varname\">dirname</var> <strong class=\"ph b synmeta\">|</strong> VALUE ( <var class=\"keyword varname\">expression</var> ) <strong class=\"ph b synmeta\">}</strong><strong class=\"ph b synmeta\">...</strong></code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n      <dl class=\"dl parml\">\n        \n          <dt class=\"dt pt dlterm\">\n            <var class=\"keyword varname\">dirname</var>\n          </dt>\n          <dd class=\"dd pd\">The name of a directory to create. If the directory already\nexists, no error is generated. If a file with this name exists,\nan error is generated. The name can be a pathname or a simple name.\nThe directory name can contain Unicode characters. See <cite class=\"cite\">OpenEdge\nDevelopment: Internationalizing Applications</cite> for more information\nabout Unicode.</dd>\n        \n      </dl>\n      <p class=\"p\">If <var class=\"keyword varname\">dirname</var> is\nnot a fully qualified directory name, ABL prepends the current working\ndirectory to <var class=\"keyword varname\">dirname.</var></p>\n      <dl class=\"dl parml\">\n        \n          <dt class=\"dt pt dlterm\">VALUE\n( <var class=\"keyword varname\">expression</var> )</dt>\n          <dd class=\"dd pd\">An expression that returns the name of a directory to create. <var class=\"keyword varname\">Expression</var> can\ncontain constants, field names, and variable names. The directory\nname can contain Unicode characters.</dd>\n        \n      </dl>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"OS-CREATE-DIR-statement__example_GC19YC2698616\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d336796e187\">Example</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">The\nfollowing procedure prompts the user for the name of a directory,\nthen creates it. If the name you give is not fully qualified, the\ndirectory is created in your current directory.</p>\n      <p class=\"p\">\n        <strong class=\"ph b\">r-os-dir.p</strong>\n      </p>\n      <table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"OS-CREATE-DIR-statement__idGDN2OQ2673671\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code>DEFINE VARIABLE stat     AS INTEGER   NO-UNDO.\nDEFINE VARIABLE dir_name AS CHARACTER NO-UNDO FORMAT &quot;x(64)&quot;\n  LABEL &quot;Enter the name of the directory you want to create.&quot;.\n\nUPDATE dir_name.\n<strong class=\"ph b\">OS-CREATE-DIR VALUE(dir_name).</strong>\nstat = OS-ERROR.\nIF stat NE 0 THEN\n  MESSAGE &quot;Directory not created. System Error #&quot; stat.</code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"OS-CREATE-DIR-statement__notes_GC19YE2698622\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d336796e225\">Notes</h2>\n      \n      <ul class=\"ul\">\n        <li class=\"li\">The\ndirectory name must conform to the naming conventions of the underlying\noperating system.</li>\n        <li class=\"li\">If a specified directory cannot be created, ABL returns an error code.</li>\n        <li class=\"li\">Although an error can occur during execution of this statement,\nthe statement does not generate an error message, raise an error\ncondition, or affect the program&#39;s flow in any way. Check for an\nexecution error by using the OS-ERROR function and evaluating the return.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"OS-CREATE-DIR-statement__see-also_GC19YF2698626\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d336796e243\">See also</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">\n        <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"OS-ERROR-function.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/OS-ERROR-function.html\">OS-ERROR function</a>\n      </p>\n    </section>\n  </div>\n<nav role=\"navigation\"><div class=\"familylinks\"><div class=\"previouslink\"><strong>Previous topic:</strong> <a class=\"link\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"OS-COPY-statement.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/OS-COPY-statement.html\">OS-COPY statement</a></div><div class=\"nextlink\"><strong>Next topic:</strong> <a class=\"link\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"OS-DELETE-statement.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/OS-DELETE-statement.html\">OS-DELETE statement</a></div></div></nav><nav class=\"related-links\" role=\"navigation\"></nav></article></main></article>\n","isWatched":false,"labelText":"Product; Product > OpenEdge; Product > OpenEdge > Version 11.7; Format; Format > Documentation","likes":0,"likeurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/like/310213","myDocsURL":null,"numOfPageViews":0,"numOfRatingsText":"<span>0 Ratings","revised":1470,"showWatch":false,"topicMeta":[["bookowner","oe11docs"],["bookrights","oe11docs"],["bundle","openedge-abl-reference-117"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product/product_openedge"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product/product_openedge/product_openedge_117"],["data","OEInformationHub/format"],["data","OEInformationHub/format/format_documentation"],["organization","oe11docs"]],"topicTitle":"OS-CREATE-DIR statement","topicurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/OS-CREATE-DIR-statement.html","type":"Manual"}